export const auditCorpusEx2Draft={"summary":{"headline":"Generation verification: structure a dev-services path on a product-heavy link-in-bio","overview":"This is a synthetic generation-verification fixture, not a live customer audit. The captured page showcases 35 products before presenting MehyarSoft services. A Start a project prompt is visible, but its clickability and delivery were not tested. There is no observed intake form, automated confirmation, or source tracking in the captured HTML. Findings are conditional structural observations applicable only if the site were deployed as a live business. The most direct structural improvement would be to verify the email route, distinguish dev-services intake from product questions, and add trust elements if owner-verified assets exist.","biggestOpportunity":"If deployed live, repositioning or anchoring the MehyarSoft offer so profile visitors with a project in mind can self-select the dev-services path without scrolling through the entire product catalog. Pairing that with a verified intake route and a permission-gated follow-up sequence could turn more page visits into qualified inquiries, though no baseline or causal effect has been measured.","startingPoint":"Run a controlled test of the Start a project email link from mobile and desktop, confirm the message reaches your inbox, and list any existing CRM, analytics, or email tools you already use so we do not duplicate effort."},"business":{"offer":"Link-in-bio hub showcasing 35 AI products including The Mayor, plus MehyarSoft custom software, AI integrations, automations, and MVP development services.","audience":"Profile visitors, local business owners, and entrepreneurs seeking custom web apps and AI builds.","serviceArea":"Brooklyn, NY"},"findings":[{"id":"F01","category":"offer","priority":"P2","title":"Clarify the dev-services path for high-intent visitors","observation":"The captured page presents 35 products before the MehyarSoft section. The description frames the page as a link-in-bio hub. A Start a project prompt appears near the MehyarSoft section, but visitors interested in custom development must scroll past the product grid to reach it.","whyItMatters":"If owner-verified analytics show that high-intent dev-services visitors leave before reaching the services section, adding an earlier self-selection path may reduce scroll friction.","recommendation":"Verify visitor intent, then consider adding a persistent top-of-page anchor letting visitors self-select between exploring products and starting a project.","nextSteps":["Verify with owner whether current traffic arrives more for product discovery or dev-services inquiries.","Confirm with owner if the Start a project prompt is visible and clickable on rendered mobile and desktop views.","Draft a variant opening line or sticky anchor for dev-services visitors, pending owner confirmation of priority."],"effort":"low","impact":"medium","confidence":"medium","citations":[{"sourceId":"S1","quote":"Page description: The link-in-bio hub for everything Mehyar Swelim builds: The Mayor, AiMech, Rizza, BabyPeek, RoastMe, Crayon Kid, jobs.mehyar, Stuff Pretty Good, Designful \u2014 plus MehyarSoft services."},{"sourceId":"S1","quote":"35 live products, one dev-services studio, zero fluff."},{"sourceId":"S1","quote":"PromptPack Pro FloodLens Playbook Clipnote Billcut Coach WattWise Memoir ValleyGods Visakit Work with me MehyarSoft Custom software &amp; AI builds Web apps, AI integrations, automations and launch-ready MVPs \u2014 designed, built and shipped by a senior systems architect."}],"measurement":{"metric":"Dev-services inquiry volume","howToCollect":"Owner logs inquiries tagged by source or landing context weekly.","currentBaseline":null,"successSignal":"Owner can report whether inquiry volume changes after any path adjustment."},"copyExample":null},{"id":"F02","category":"journey","priority":"P2","title":"Build a permission-gated follow-up sequence for dev-services leads","observation":"The page lists an email address and Start a project prompt but shows no automated confirmation or next-step explanation in the captured text. The only list-building mechanism is The drop list newsletter. Any follow-up pilot would need recorded permission.","whyItMatters":"Without a defined next step after inquiry, warm leads may cool while waiting for a response. A follow-up sequence could improve readiness, but only with verified permission.","recommendation":"Create a brief, permission-based follow-up route for dev-services inquiries that confirms receipt and outlines next steps, gated by verified opt-in.","nextSteps":["Verify existing email tools and CRM with owner; confirm no duplicate systems.","Verify recorded customer permission for dev-services follow-up and explicitly exclude declined, withdrawn, and unverified contacts.","Confirm timing, capacity, and final wording with owner; replace all placeholders; test delivery and reply route with staff or dummy records.","Contact only the verified-permission pilot cohort, then record delivery, replies, opt-outs, and resulting appointments separately."],"effort":"medium","impact":"medium","confidence":"medium","citations":[{"sourceId":"S1","quote":"Start a project \u2192 Contact [email&#160;protected] DM on Instagram The drop list New launches hit your inbox first."},{"sourceId":"S1","quote":"One email a month, no noise."}],"measurement":{"metric":"Follow-up pilot outcomes","howToCollect":"For the eligible verified-permission cohort, record sent date, delivery confirmations, replies, opt-outs, and any appointments booked within a 30-day window.","currentBaseline":null,"successSignal":"Owner observes bounded reply and opt-out rates from the pilot cohort without promising causal uplift."},"copyExample":"Subject: Got your project note \u2014 what happens next\n\nThanks for reaching out about a build. I reply to every message personally. If you haven\u2019t heard back within [verified hours], feel free to nudge me on [verified social handle].\n\nTypical next step: a [verified call length] call to confirm scope and timeline. No pitch, just clarity."},{"id":"F03","category":"trust","priority":"P2","title":"Verify existing trust assets for the MehyarSoft section","observation":"The captured excerpt shows product names and a services description, including designed, built and shipped by a senior systems architect. Independent trust signals such as client testimonials or case studies were not observed in the captured text and remain unknown.","whyItMatters":"Prospects evaluating custom builds may look for social proof specific to client work. If such assets exist, displaying them could support credibility.","recommendation":"Ask the owner to verify whether client testimonials, case studies, or public portfolio pieces exist, then add one verified trust element to the MehyarSoft section if available.","nextSteps":["Ask owner to verify whether client testimonials, case studies, or public portfolio pieces exist in owner records or on unobserved pages.","If verified assets exist, draft one concise case-study snippet or process summary using confirmed project details only.","If no client work can be shared publicly, draft a How I work paragraph explaining discovery, build, and handoff phases for owner review."],"effort":"low","impact":"medium","confidence":"medium","citations":[{"sourceId":"S1","quote":"Mehyar Swelim @mehyar.us I build AI products that ship."},{"sourceId":"S1","quote":"PromptPack Pro FloodLens Playbook Clipnote Billcut Coach WattWise Memoir ValleyGods Visakit Work with me MehyarSoft Custom software &amp; AI builds Web apps, AI integrations, automations and launch-ready MVPs \u2014 designed, built and shipped by a senior systems architect."},{"sourceId":"S1","quote":"If you have an idea, I can have it live."}],"measurement":{"metric":"Presence of service-specific trust content","howToCollect":"Owner inspects the MehyarSoft section and counts distinct verified trust elements such as testimonials, case snippets, or process steps.","currentBaseline":null,"successSignal":"MehyarSoft section contains at least one owner-verified trust element specific to client engagements."},"copyExample":null},{"id":"F04","category":"conversion","priority":"P1","title":"Test the Start a project intake route end to end","observation":"The page shows a Start a project prompt followed by Contact [email&#160;protected] and DM on Instagram. The email address appears with an HTML entity. No contact form or booking calendar is visible in the captured text. The observed formCount may belong to the newsletter.","whyItMatters":"If the email link is not clickable or the HTML entity breaks mailto behavior, visitors may abandon the attempt. The actual delivery path is untested.","recommendation":"Verify that the Start a project path results in a delivered message through an owner-authorized controlled test before changing the page.","nextSteps":["Owner performs an authorized controlled test: click Start a project from mobile and desktop, verify the email client opens with a valid recipient, and confirm the message reaches the inbox and spam folder.","Verify with owner whether any existing form builder or intake tool is already available before creating a new form.","If the email route fails or is cumbersome, draft a clickable mailto link or a short intake form for the MehyarSoft section for owner approval.","Verify with owner who monitors the Instagram DM inbox and what typical response time is."],"effort":"low","impact":"high","confidence":"high","citations":[{"sourceId":"S1","quote":"Start a project \u2192 Contact [email&#160;protected] DM on Instagram The drop list New launches hit your inbox first."}],"measurement":{"metric":"Successful test sends from the Start a project path","howToCollect":"Owner sends test messages from both mobile and desktop, then checks inbox and spam folders for receipt.","currentBaseline":null,"successSignal":"Both test messages arrive in the owner inbox without user-side errors."},"copyExample":null},{"id":"F05","category":"operations","priority":"P2","title":"Clarify internal routing between product interest and dev-services inquiries","observation":"The page promotes The Mayor as a flagship product for local businesses alongside MehyarSoft custom builds. The same contact points appear to handle both product questions and custom project requests.","whyItMatters":"Mixed inquiries could create manual sorting work and delay responses if the owner must triage product support versus high-intent dev-services leads.","recommendation":"Distinguish the intake path for MehyarSoft inquiries from general product questions, either through a dedicated subject line, form field, or separate contact channel.","nextSteps":["Verify with owner how incoming emails and DMs are currently categorized and whether dev-services leads are tagged differently.","Add a subject-line prompt or form dropdown asking Product question / Project inquiry / Partnership so the owner can prioritize at a glance.","If volume supports it, create a dedicated project-inquiry email alias or scheduling link for discovery calls."],"effort":"low","impact":"medium","confidence":"medium","citations":[{"sourceId":"S1","quote":"Your front desk for local business \u2014 missed calls answered by text-back, appointments booked, customers followed up."},{"sourceId":"S1","quote":"PromptPack Pro FloodLens Playbook Clipnote Billcut Coach WattWise Memoir ValleyGods Visakit Work with me MehyarSoft Custom software &amp; AI builds Web apps, AI integrations, automations and launch-ready MVPs \u2014 designed, built and shipped by a senior systems architect."},{"sourceId":"S1","quote":"Start a project \u2192 Contact [email&#160;protected] DM on Instagram The drop list New launches hit your inbox first."}],"measurement":{"metric":"Inquiry categorization accuracy","howToCollect":"Owner reviews a sample of recent messages and tags them by intent such as product, project, or partnership.","currentBaseline":null,"successSignal":"Owner can sort new inquiries by intent without opening each thread."},"copyExample":null},{"id":"F06","category":"measurement","priority":"P2","title":"Add lightweight source tracking to the Start a project path","observation":"The page may receive profile visitors from multiple channels, but no visible UTM parameters, referral tracking, or channel-specific landing variants are present in the captured HTML. The owner cannot currently distinguish a dev-services inquiry that came from the link-in-bio versus other sources.","whyItMatters":"Without knowing which traffic turns into inquiries, the owner cannot decide whether to optimize the page for product discovery or for client acquisition.","recommendation":"Add lightweight source identification to the Start a project path so the owner can correlate inquiries with their origin.","nextSteps":["Verify existing analytics or tracking tools with owner before adding new scripts.","If no adequate tool exists, add a hidden source field to any intake form, or use a dedicated link for the Instagram bio that leads to the MehyarSoft section.","Log each inquiry with its self-reported or URL-reported source in a simple spreadsheet."],"effort":"low","impact":"medium","confidence":"medium","citations":[{"sourceId":"S1","quote":"Page description: The link-in-bio hub for everything Mehyar Swelim builds: The Mayor, AiMech, Rizza, BabyPeek, RoastMe, Crayon Kid, jobs.mehyar, Stuff Pretty Good, Designful \u2014 plus MehyarSoft services."},{"sourceId":"S1","quote":"Start a project \u2192 Contact [email&#160;protected] DM on Instagram The drop list New launches hit your inbox first."}],"measurement":{"metric":"Inquiry source mix","howToCollect":"Owner records source or channel for each dev-services inquiry over a 30-day window.","currentBaseline":null,"successSignal":"Owner can report the share of inquiries attributed to the link-in-bio page versus other channels."},"copyExample":null}],"roadmap":[{"window":"30_days","objective":"Verify existing tools, intake routes, and traffic intent before adding new systems.","findingIds":["F01","F04","F05","F06"],"ownerRole":"Studio owner","deliverables":["[F01,F04,F05,F06] Studio owner lists all existing analytics, CRM, email, and intake tools currently in use.","[F01] Studio owner confirms whether traffic arrives more for product discovery or dev-services inquiries.","[F04] Studio owner tests the Start a project email route from mobile and desktop and confirms inbox and spam-folder delivery.","[F05] Studio owner documents how dev-services and product inquiries are currently categorized and responded to."]},{"window":"60_days","objective":"Clarify the services offer and add trust elements to the MehyarSoft section.","findingIds":["F01","F03","F05"],"ownerRole":"Studio owner","deliverables":["[F01] Studio owner adds a persistent Start a project anchor or repositions the MehyarSoft section based on verified traffic intent.","[F03] Studio owner drafts and adds one verified case study, testimonial, or process summary to the MehyarSoft section.","[F05] Studio owner implements an inquiry tag or subject-line prompt to separate project leads from product questions."]},{"window":"90_days","objective":"Launch permission-gated follow-up and source tracking for dev-services inquiries.","findingIds":["F02","F06"],"ownerRole":"Studio owner","deliverables":["[F02] Studio owner verifies recorded permission and excludes declined, withdrawn, and unverified contacts before any follow-up.","[F02] Studio owner confirms timing, capacity, and final wording; replaces all placeholders; tests delivery and reply route with staff or dummy records.","[F02] Studio owner sends the follow-up sequence only to the verified-permission pilot cohort and records delivery, replies, opt-outs, and appointments.","[F06] Studio owner adds source tracking to the Start a project path and logs inquiry origins for 30 days."]}],"unknowns":["Whether the single observed form belongs to the newsletter or a project intake path.","Whether any private CRM, analytics, or email automation tools exist behind the public page.","The actual monthly volume of profile visitors and how many currently convert to dev-services inquiries.","Whether Instagram DM is actively monitored for business inquiries and what response time is typical.","Whether The Mayor product generates support traffic that mixes with MehyarSoft leads in the same inbox.","Whether client case studies or testimonials exist but are simply not rendered in the captured HTML.","Whether the Start a project prompt is clickable on rendered mobile and desktop views.","Whether the displayed email address resolves correctly when clicked due to the HTML entity encoding."],"questionsToResolve":["Do you currently use any email marketing, CRM, or analytics tools behind this page?","Which channel drives more profile visitors: Instagram bio, direct referrals, or organic search?","Have you worked with dev-services clients whose outcomes can be shared as case studies?","Who monitors the displayed contact inbox and what is your typical response time?","Is the observed form functional for newsletter signups, and is the list actively used?","What is your current capacity for new dev-services projects each month?","Have you recorded explicit opt-in permission from past dev-services leads for follow-up emails?"]};

